WEBVTT

00:01.296 --> 00:05.016
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.017 --> 00:08.252
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.253 --> 00:11.923
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.924 --> 00:14.691
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.692 --> 00:18.196
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.197 --> 00:21.733
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.734 --> 00:23.267
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.268 --> 00:24.843
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.844 --> 00:30.209
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:36.073 --> 00:38.264
Ugh! This sucks, Mom.

00:38.265 --> 00:40.888
We really have to spend the whole day
cleaning out the garage?

00:40.889 --> 00:42.078
Yeah, come on, Lois.

00:42.079 --> 00:44.881
<i>You know I have plans today
to go see Pervert Hamlet.</i>

00:44.882 --> 00:45.914
To be...

00:45.915 --> 00:48.501
with this skull sexually,

00:48.502 --> 00:50.052
or not to be...

00:50.053 --> 00:52.515
with this skull sexually.

00:52.516 --> 00:54.390
That is the question...

00:54.391 --> 00:58.318
I answered when I was
with this skull sexually

00:58.319 --> 01:00.397
a little while ago.

01:01.931 --> 01:04.634
Huh. All these spray paint cans
are empty.

01:04.635 --> 01:06.903
What? Really?

01:06.904 --> 01:08.938
H-How could such a thing

01:08.939 --> 01:10.942
have come to pass?

01:13.076 --> 01:14.944
Screw this. Quick,
before your mother gets back,

01:14.945 --> 01:16.245
everything in the garbage.

01:16.246 --> 01:17.748
We're throwing all this stuff out.

01:23.317 --> 01:25.450
Wait. You're throwing away
Stewie's Big Wheel?

01:25.451 --> 01:27.119
Relax. It's not even his.

01:27.120 --> 01:29.624
I took it from a front lawn
after a rain storm.

01:33.427 --> 01:36.615
I thought they'd never leave,
Factory Red.

01:40.499 --> 01:42.610
So, I guess Thanos got the Mind Stone.

01:42.611 --> 01:44.047
Wow. So now he's got all of 'em.

01:44.048 --> 01:46.172
- I guess so.
- What does that mean for us?

01:46.173 --> 01:47.811
I have no idea.

01:48.250 --> 01:50.498
I knew it was gonna be us.

01:51.887 --> 01:55.457
Oh, my God. There's a hot woman
over at the bar.

01:56.219 --> 01:58.092
You know, I never forget
the back of a head.

01:58.093 --> 02:00.795
I don't think we've met.
I'm Glenn Quagmire.

02:00.796 --> 02:02.731
I'm sure that kind of thing works great

02:02.732 --> 02:05.267
for the younger crowd, but I'm 44.

02:05.268 --> 02:07.735
44? Oh-ho, why am I trying so hard?

02:07.736 --> 02:09.404
Come on, let's get out of here.

02:09.405 --> 02:12.643
Look, I'm not some bimbo who
falls for tired pickup lines.

02:14.144 --> 02:15.911
Wow. That was painful.

02:15.912 --> 02:18.913
Like that time I passed
a kidney Stone Phillips.

02:18.914 --> 02:20.414
Oh!

02:20.415 --> 02:22.084
Aah! Aah!

02:23.286 --> 02:25.923
Or was it... murder?

02:29.324 --> 02:31.259
- Hey, Doug.
- Hey, Stewie.

02:31.260 --> 02:33.162
Taking the Big Wheel out for a spin?

02:33.163 --> 02:34.429
Yep. Where are you headed?

02:34.430 --> 02:36.597
Oh, I was just gonna
drive through some puddles

02:36.598 --> 02:38.299
and see how long my tracks stay wet.

02:38.300 --> 02:41.269
The record is seven sidewalk
squares, by yours truly.

02:41.270 --> 02:42.937
Allegedly.

02:42.938 --> 02:44.942
Okay, get out of here, you nut.

02:47.943 --> 02:50.346
What the deuce? Where is it?

02:58.187 --> 03:01.190
Boy, I tell ya,
no better way to start your day

03:01.191 --> 03:03.191
than a morning dump
in a neighbor's yard.

03:03.192 --> 03:04.692
Come on, Brian!

03:04.693 --> 03:07.863
It was a soft steamer,
almost impossible to pick up.

03:07.864 --> 03:09.798
Brian, have you seen my Big Wheel?

03:09.799 --> 03:11.199
I can't find it anywhere!

03:11.200 --> 03:12.501
What? No. Did you look...?

03:12.502 --> 03:13.869
Oh, wait a minute.

03:13.870 --> 03:15.971
Peter threw out a bunch of stuff
from the garage yesterday.

03:15.972 --> 03:17.471
Maybe it was in there.

03:17.472 --> 03:21.144
Threw it out? But today
is our trash pick up day!

03:22.878 --> 03:24.534
We're too late!

03:24.535 --> 03:26.048
I've got to get that Big Wheel back.

03:26.049 --> 03:27.882
Will you drive me to the town dump?

03:27.883 --> 03:30.552
Really? Can't we just maybe
buy you a new one?

03:30.553 --> 03:32.387
No, Brian. It has to be that Big Wheel.

03:32.388 --> 03:34.388
It's very special to me.

03:34.389 --> 03:36.191
I lost my V-card on that thing.

03:36.192 --> 03:37.692
You what?

03:37.693 --> 03:40.561
Yep, went over a speed bump
really fast and broke my hymen.

03:40.562 --> 03:42.030
Stewie, you don't have a hymen.

03:42.031 --> 03:44.066
- Yeah, not anymore.
- No, you're a boy.

03:44.067 --> 03:46.668
I have to correct you there,
Brian. I'm a man.

03:46.669 --> 03:48.336
'Cause, you know... broken hymen.

03:48.337 --> 03:50.172
Boys don't have hymens!

03:50.173 --> 03:52.840
Okay, then I may have just
ripped my taint.

03:52.841 --> 03:55.077
Either way, I love that bike!

04:00.048 --> 04:01.350
Hi. Can you help us?

04:01.351 --> 04:03.184
We're trying to locate a lost Big Wh...

04:03.185 --> 04:04.720
My God,

04:04.721 --> 04:06.722
there's just so...

04:06.723 --> 04:08.924
much... garbage.

04:12.262 --> 04:14.395
Yes, we are in search of a Big Wheel

04:14.396 --> 04:17.032
that was erroneously discarded
and collected today.

04:17.033 --> 04:20.701
Oh, then it probably came in
with the morning load.

04:20.702 --> 04:23.071
Sorry. That term always makes me blush.

04:23.072 --> 04:26.275
But if it just came in, that's bad news.

04:26.276 --> 04:28.710
Usually the newest, top layer of trash

04:28.711 --> 04:30.781
just blows right into the ocean.

04:34.951 --> 04:37.953
Yeah, I'm afraid your Big Wheel
may be gones for good.

04:37.954 --> 04:40.289
Dear God, this is horrible!

04:40.290 --> 04:42.391
I'm blind! I'm blind! I'm blind!

04:43.558 --> 04:46.962
Phew. Ooh, something smells good
in this box.

04:46.963 --> 04:49.600
I'm blind! I'm blind! I'm blind!

04:54.240 --> 04:57.138
Damn it. Monica's not responding
to any of my texts.

04:57.139 --> 04:59.640
You're still trying
to bang that 44-year-old?

04:59.641 --> 05:01.143
- What are you sending her?
- Mostly porn.

05:01.144 --> 05:02.477
Just shots of rods.

05:02.478 --> 05:04.746
All angles. Up, down, left, right.

05:04.747 --> 05:07.749
Lois, maybe you could help me
ask out this woman I met.

05:07.750 --> 05:09.326
She's close to your age.

05:09.327 --> 05:11.152
But she won't respond
to any of my texts.

05:11.153 --> 05:12.487
Oh, well, that's easy.

05:12.488 --> 05:15.324
<i>Just ask her if she's all
caught up on This Is Us.</i>

05:17.993 --> 05:20.996
She says, "I'm one behind,
so no spoilers.

05:20.997 --> 05:24.633
Hysterical laughing face,
hysterical laughing face."

05:24.634 --> 05:26.167
How-how is that funny?

05:26.168 --> 05:27.602
It's not, but you're in.

05:27.603 --> 05:30.004
Great. This is exactly
the stuff I need to know.

05:30.005 --> 05:33.174
Lois, will you teach me the ways
of the middle-aged woman?

05:33.175 --> 05:35.477
All right. I'm a sucker for romance.

05:35.478 --> 05:38.313
Thanks, Lois. This could open up
a whole new world for me.

05:38.314 --> 05:40.448
Like one of those kids who gets a device

05:40.449 --> 05:42.952
that allows them to hear
for the first time.

05:43.985 --> 05:47.289
- Billy, can you hear?
- Yes!

05:47.290 --> 05:50.303
Amazing! This is amazing.

05:50.304 --> 05:52.027
Your mom and I are going
to get a divorce.

05:52.028 --> 05:53.494
I'm in love with someone else,

05:53.495 --> 05:56.299
and I didn't want
to say it with the silly hands.

06:01.065 --> 06:03.003
Brian, I've been doing research
on my Big Wheel.

06:03.004 --> 06:04.705
If it ended up in the ocean,

06:04.706 --> 06:07.174
it most likely has traveled
to Garbage Island.

06:07.175 --> 06:08.876
What's Garbage Island?

06:08.877 --> 06:11.713
The other name for the
North Atlantic Garbage Patch,

06:11.714 --> 06:13.381
an enormous cluster of man-made debris

06:13.382 --> 06:15.350
floating in the middle of the ocean.

06:15.351 --> 06:17.318
This is terrible.
We got to raise awareness,

06:17.319 --> 06:19.186
- let people know about it.
- I agree.

06:19.187 --> 06:21.619
<i>It's like a giant garbage whirlpool.</i>

06:23.326 --> 06:24.603
Brian?

06:26.219 --> 06:27.496
You heard me.

06:27.497 --> 06:29.864
Anyway, I'm heading there
to find my Big Wheel.

06:29.865 --> 06:31.165
Perhaps you'll come with me.

06:31.166 --> 06:32.734
Boating to an island of garbage?

06:32.735 --> 06:35.035
I'm in. Maybe Peter will come, too.

06:35.036 --> 06:37.172
Hey, Peter, want to go on a boat ride?

06:37.173 --> 06:40.708
Oh, uh, I can't be in stories
for a couple of episodes.

06:40.709 --> 06:43.045
I'm real-life pregnant.

06:44.247 --> 06:46.080
Oh, my God. I had no idea.

06:46.081 --> 06:47.349
I know!

06:47.350 --> 06:49.920
Anyway, Mama's got to get off her feet.

06:57.259 --> 07:00.595
All right, time to retrieve my
Big Wheel from Garbage Island.

07:00.596 --> 07:02.763
Let's do it.

07:02.764 --> 07:05.032
Hey, how'd you get the money
to rent this boat anyway?

07:05.033 --> 07:07.370
Oh, I got a part-time job at Target.

07:11.740 --> 07:15.109
Okay, technically, I work at
the weird, in-store Pizza Hut.

07:15.110 --> 07:17.044
<i>The Target In-Store Pizza Hut.</i>

07:17.045 --> 07:20.916
<i>Feed it to your fat kid while
you buy off-brand tennis shoes.</i>

07:24.553 --> 07:26.955
Now, Glenn, I'm gonna help you
get into the mind

07:26.956 --> 07:28.390
of a middle-aged woman.

07:28.391 --> 07:31.393
We all go frigging
nuts over Yankee Candles,

07:31.394 --> 07:34.563
so to help you learn all the
flavors, I made a little quiz.

07:34.564 --> 07:36.965
I'm gonna give you a name,
and you tell me

07:36.966 --> 07:39.734
if it's the name of
a Yankee Candle or a porn star.

07:39.735 --> 07:41.970
- Okay.
- Black Coconut.

07:41.971 --> 07:43.237
Porn star?

07:43.238 --> 07:46.073
No, that's a candle. Amber Gold.

07:46.074 --> 07:48.576
<i>- Candle?
- That is a candle.</i>

07:48.577 --> 07:50.578
April Showers.

07:50.579 --> 07:52.580
Um... both?

07:52.581 --> 07:56.751
Very good. I tried to trick you
there, but you got it. Both.

07:56.752 --> 07:58.419
Okay, okay, I'm writing this all down.

07:58.420 --> 08:01.489
But, Lois, Monica agreed
to have dinner with me tomorrow.

08:01.490 --> 08:03.924
- That's great!
- I suppose.

08:03.925 --> 08:06.294
But I don't think
I can pull it off by myself.

08:06.295 --> 08:07.828
Will you come and just be nearby

08:07.829 --> 08:09.830
to give me tips and help me
get through it?

08:09.831 --> 08:12.100
Fine, but I'll have
to rearrange my schedule.

08:12.101 --> 08:14.335
Friday nights are when
Peter and I do edibles

08:14.336 --> 08:16.005
and go to the aquarium.

08:19.442 --> 08:21.442
This is awesome.

08:21.443 --> 08:23.845
Peter, I'm freaking out.

08:23.846 --> 08:26.649
Yeah, don't-don't...
don't ruin it for me.

08:36.458 --> 08:39.960
Okay, I spy something blue.

08:39.961 --> 08:42.663
Uh... the ocean?

08:42.664 --> 08:44.132
Nope.

08:44.133 --> 08:45.466
The sky?

08:45.467 --> 08:47.134
Hey, you got it in two, bud.

08:47.135 --> 08:48.302
That ties the record.

08:48.303 --> 08:49.503
Stewie, I'm starting to wonder

08:49.504 --> 08:51.639
if we didn't think this
all the way through.

08:51.640 --> 08:52.974
No, it's fine.

08:52.975 --> 08:55.161
It'll all be worth it
once we get to Garbage Island.

08:56.211 --> 08:58.146
Not a lot of wind today.

08:58.147 --> 08:59.714
No.

08:59.715 --> 09:01.483
Hey, what causes wind?

09:01.484 --> 09:03.718
Well, if my reading material
has taught me anything,

09:03.719 --> 09:06.156
it's just a cloud with lips.

09:08.224 --> 09:10.225
Blustery...

09:10.226 --> 09:12.027
is a good word.

09:12.028 --> 09:13.494
Uh-huh.

09:13.495 --> 09:16.196
<i>Mm... Moana.</i>

09:16.899 --> 09:19.500
Mm.

09:20.243 --> 09:21.908
<i>I never saw Moana.</i>

09:22.837 --> 09:26.277
<i>You never saw Moana?</i>

09:51.767 --> 09:53.268
Your blowout looks nice.

09:53.269 --> 09:54.702
Oh, thanks.

09:54.703 --> 09:58.205
So, um, I noticed a yoga mat
in the back of your car.

09:58.206 --> 10:00.777
How often do you do yoga?

10:13.755 --> 10:15.389
- Is everything all right?
- Hmm?

10:15.390 --> 10:16.725
Oh, oh, yeah, yeah. Sorry.

10:16.726 --> 10:19.561
My, um... my-my dad
locked himself out of his car.

10:19.562 --> 10:21.562
Oh, sorry. Do you need to help him?

10:21.563 --> 10:23.431
Um, no, uh, no. He, um, he broke, uh...

10:23.432 --> 10:24.798
broke the window with his foot.

10:24.799 --> 10:27.067
High heel. My dad's a woman now.

10:27.068 --> 10:29.605
Oh.

10:36.578 --> 10:38.245
You're lucky we came here.

10:38.246 --> 10:39.980
I almost suggested Mickey D's.

10:39.981 --> 10:42.617
Oh, my God.

10:42.618 --> 10:43.984
That's so informal.

10:43.985 --> 10:45.653
Are you talking about McDonald's?

10:45.654 --> 10:47.287
Yeah, yeah!

10:47.288 --> 10:49.490
Another thing
I was just thinking about is...

10:49.491 --> 10:51.426
"AMBER Alert, white Honda Accord,

10:51.427 --> 10:53.260
license plate..." Uh, uh, I mean,

10:53.261 --> 10:56.096
Pinterest sure has
some neat pictures of sinks.

10:56.097 --> 10:57.666
Doesn't it?

10:57.667 --> 10:59.834
Listen, what if we just bail on dinner

10:59.835 --> 11:01.635
and head back to my place?

11:01.636 --> 11:02.838
Great! I'm in.

11:08.510 --> 11:10.698
Wait! You have to pay for the bread.

11:10.699 --> 11:11.908
Hey!

11:12.814 --> 11:15.317
You have to pay for the bread!

11:17.186 --> 11:18.853
You have to pay for the bread!

11:18.854 --> 11:21.188
You have to pay for the bread!

11:21.189 --> 11:22.456
The bread!

11:22.457 --> 11:24.993
You have to pay

11:24.994 --> 11:26.661
for the bread!

11:36.371 --> 11:38.307
Moana?

11:42.662 --> 11:45.048
Oh, my God. Brian. Look!

11:49.217 --> 11:50.851
We made it!

11:50.852 --> 11:52.986
We made it to Garbage Island!

11:52.987 --> 11:55.223
My God, I don't believe it.

11:55.224 --> 11:57.691
Whoa, look at all the packaging
from Mickey D's.

11:57.692 --> 11:59.694
What? Oh, my God, I've never heard that.

11:59.695 --> 12:02.162
"Mickey D's." That is just great.

12:02.163 --> 12:04.364
Anyway, let's start looking
for my Big Wheel.

12:04.365 --> 12:07.000
Hey, check it out,
a VCR just sitting here.

12:07.001 --> 12:09.037
I'm taking this sucker home.

12:15.376 --> 12:17.959
- Oh, crap.
- Brian, you idiot.

12:17.960 --> 12:20.103
Now how the hell are we supposed
to get back to land?

12:20.104 --> 12:21.790
We're both going to die.

12:21.791 --> 12:25.164
Oh, look, a message in a bottle
is washing up.

12:25.165 --> 12:26.755
Maybe this'll help.

12:27.856 --> 12:29.758
<i>PETER: DEAR ENGLAND: Enclosed,</i>

12:29.759 --> 12:33.427
<i>please find one bottle fart
in exchange for Russell Brand.</i>

12:33.428 --> 12:35.864
<i>We feel this is
appropriate compensation.</i>

12:35.865 --> 12:38.099
<i>Yours, et cetera, America.</i>

12:47.876 --> 12:50.254
Damn it, Brian!
How could you sink our boat?

12:50.255 --> 12:51.543
We're going to die!

12:51.544 --> 12:53.104
You guys need any help?

12:53.105 --> 12:55.044
- Aah!
- Aah! Who the hell are you?

12:55.045 --> 12:56.754
Name's Taylor. 'Sup?

12:56.755 --> 12:57.989
How the hell did you get here?

12:57.990 --> 13:00.812
Oh, I, uh...
I-I fell off a booze cruise.

13:00.813 --> 13:03.355
- You what?
- Yep, washed up here.

13:03.356 --> 13:05.060
Matter of fact, we all did.

13:08.129 --> 13:10.431
How are you all planning
to get back home?

13:10.432 --> 13:13.190
Get back home?
Why would we want to do that?

13:13.191 --> 13:15.916
Yeah, we've got everything we need here.

13:15.917 --> 13:19.107
There's tons of free,
half-eaten food that washes up.

13:19.108 --> 13:21.744
And we just bang each other all day.

13:21.745 --> 13:23.379
That, uh...

13:23.380 --> 13:25.195
that doesn't sound terrible.

13:25.196 --> 13:28.250
Hey, so, we've been stuck
out here for over 20 years.

13:28.251 --> 13:30.119
Can you catch us up
on all the important things

13:30.120 --> 13:31.288
that we've missed?

13:36.959 --> 13:38.126
So, no way!

13:38.127 --> 13:40.462
Kylie Jenner and Tyga
are no longer together?

13:40.463 --> 13:41.963
Splitsville, my friend.

13:41.964 --> 13:44.232
How did Robert Kardashian die?

13:44.233 --> 13:46.401
- Guilt cancer.
- From what?

13:46.402 --> 13:47.904
Oh, boy.

13:52.390 --> 13:55.627
So people thought the dancing
Judge Itos were funny?

13:55.628 --> 13:56.628
For a while, yes.

13:56.629 --> 13:58.196
Is Leno still doing it?

13:58.197 --> 13:59.797
No, he's not hosting anymore.

13:59.798 --> 14:01.867
<i>Oh, so Conan got The Tonight Show?</i>

14:01.868 --> 14:03.537
Oh, come o...

14:08.709 --> 14:11.143
A-And so what about
Craig Kilborn? Is he still on?

14:11.144 --> 14:12.476
I'm actually right here.

14:12.477 --> 14:14.618
Oh, right. Hey, Craig.

14:21.236 --> 14:22.387
Oh, hi, Glenn.

14:22.388 --> 14:23.989
I haven't seen you in a while.

14:23.990 --> 14:25.556
H-How are things with Monica?

14:25.557 --> 14:26.725
Who?

14:26.726 --> 14:29.393
Monica, y-your hot date
from the other night.

14:29.394 --> 14:31.062
Oh, yeah. I plowed her. Thanks again.

14:31.063 --> 14:33.231
But-but I thought she was the one.

14:33.232 --> 14:34.499
Yeah, no, what I realized is

14:34.500 --> 14:36.067
that all those texts you sent me,

14:36.068 --> 14:37.402
they're like my bible now.

14:37.403 --> 14:40.004
I just keep using these
same tips on different women.

14:40.005 --> 14:41.406
I owe you, Lois.

14:41.407 --> 14:44.576
You've opened up a whole world
of middle-aged legs to me.

14:46.245 --> 14:49.715
Oh, my God. Quagmire's
terrorizing middle-aged women,

14:49.716 --> 14:51.682
and I'm responsible for it.

14:51.683 --> 14:53.746
I've created a monster.

14:58.191 --> 15:01.093
Oh, no! My Luna Bar for women.

15:13.873 --> 15:15.706
Please call the DWP.

15:15.707 --> 15:17.276
I'm stuck in here.

15:24.616 --> 15:26.618
Hey, what day is it?

15:26.619 --> 15:28.085
Trash day.

15:30.623 --> 15:32.758
Brian, look, I found my Big Wheel.

15:32.759 --> 15:34.960
- Cool.
- It's more than cool, Brian.

15:34.961 --> 15:37.461
I believe the Big Wheel
may actually be our ticket

15:37.462 --> 15:38.629
off the island.

15:38.630 --> 15:39.965
You see, I've calculated that,

15:39.966 --> 15:41.399
even with both of our weights,

15:41.400 --> 15:43.234
it will still be capable of flotation.

15:43.235 --> 15:44.735
My plan is to attach

15:44.736 --> 15:47.071
six Jimmy Buffett
margarita machines to it,

15:47.072 --> 15:49.307
which should be able to propel us home.

15:49.308 --> 15:51.810
Home? I don't think I want to go home.

15:51.811 --> 15:53.811
What? What are you talking about?

15:53.812 --> 15:56.148
I'm saying I like it here
on Garbage Island.

15:56.149 --> 15:57.983
O-Okay, I-I don't think
I can talk to you,

15:57.984 --> 15:59.484
because, right now,
you're making less sense

15:59.485 --> 16:01.820
than an M.C. Escher floor plan.

16:01.821 --> 16:04.288
So, how's it coming?

16:04.289 --> 16:06.157
Are we gonna finish on schedule?

16:06.158 --> 16:07.426
I don't know, Mr. Escher.

16:07.427 --> 16:09.760
I've never put six stairways
all in one spot.

16:09.761 --> 16:11.662
And I've lost, like,
ten of my guys in here.

16:11.663 --> 16:13.933
Hey, I need a hammer!

16:15.182 --> 16:17.926
I hate this place! I quit!

16:25.755 --> 16:28.346
Uh, 'scuse me, I'm-I'm looking
for anything by...

16:28.347 --> 16:29.681
Mike "Bubble"?

16:29.682 --> 16:31.682
It's "BublГ©," you idiot!

16:31.683 --> 16:33.317
Oh, hey, Lo... Ow!

16:33.318 --> 16:34.820
That feels great!

16:34.821 --> 16:37.489
Glenn Quagmire, I tried
to help you meet a nice woman,

16:37.490 --> 16:39.691
but you just couldn't help
yourself, could you?

16:39.692 --> 16:41.026
What are you talking about?

16:41.027 --> 16:42.960
I thought I was helping you find love,

16:42.961 --> 16:44.796
and, instead, you used me as a tool

16:44.797 --> 16:47.699
to get down every middle-aged
woman's pants in town.

16:47.700 --> 16:49.534
Slacks, Lois. They call them slacks.

16:49.535 --> 16:52.170
You wouldn't know that
if it wasn't for me!

16:52.171 --> 16:53.704
You're right.

16:53.705 --> 16:56.474
You were kind to me,
and I took advantage of it.

16:56.475 --> 16:58.463
I owe you an apology.

16:58.464 --> 17:00.498
Well, thank you.

17:00.499 --> 17:02.012
Here, let me make it up to you.

17:02.013 --> 17:04.149
I'll buy you a coffee, and...

17:04.150 --> 17:06.218
do you like the music of Ray...

17:06.219 --> 17:07.551
"LaMountain"?

17:07.552 --> 17:08.886
"LaMontagne."

17:08.887 --> 17:10.721
Thank you. Hey, beautiful,

17:10.722 --> 17:12.891
you want to take
a pointless girl-stride walk

17:12.892 --> 17:14.992
and listen to Ray LaMontagne?

17:14.993 --> 17:16.394
- Sure.
- Great.

17:16.395 --> 17:17.854
See ya, Lois.

17:21.500 --> 17:22.834
Last chance, Brian.

17:22.835 --> 17:24.744
You're really not coming with me?

17:24.745 --> 17:26.505
I'm sorry, Stewie. I'm not.

17:26.506 --> 17:28.172
I know it's weird to say, but...

17:28.173 --> 17:30.674
it's kind of just too perfect
for me here.

17:30.675 --> 17:31.876
I see.

17:31.877 --> 17:33.377
Well, I should go.

17:33.378 --> 17:35.846
Fort Lauderdale Tanya found
a four-piece puzzle

17:35.847 --> 17:37.015
she's been struggling with.

17:37.016 --> 17:38.849
Where does the cow go?

17:38.850 --> 17:40.585
It's all corners, babe.

17:40.586 --> 17:42.536
I have to say,

17:42.537 --> 17:45.257
I never imagined
saying goodbye to you, Brian.

17:45.258 --> 17:47.705
So long take very good care

17:47.706 --> 17:49.994
dear friend of mine farewell.

17:49.995 --> 17:51.363
That's odd phrasing.

17:51.364 --> 17:53.230
Sorry, it's been hard to think straight.

17:53.231 --> 17:56.201
From the moment we arrived,
I've either been drunk or ejaculating.

17:56.202 --> 17:58.769
These are things
you don't say to a baby.

17:58.770 --> 18:00.739
Goodbye, Brian.

18:00.740 --> 18:02.740
Goodbye, Stewie.

18:25.431 --> 18:29.633
<i>Sha-la-la-la-la-la, my lady</i>

18:29.634 --> 18:33.305
<i>In the sun with your hair undone</i>

18:33.306 --> 18:34.972
<i>Can you hear me now</i>

18:34.973 --> 18:39.479
<i>Callin' your name from across the bay?</i>

18:40.980 --> 18:44.783
<i>A summer's day laughin' and a-hidin'</i>

18:44.784 --> 18:49.954
<i>Chasin' love out on Thunder Island</i>

18:49.955 --> 18:52.289
<i>Do-do-do, do-do-do</i>

18:52.290 --> 18:54.291
<i>Do-do-do-do-do</i>

18:55.760 --> 18:58.329
<i>Do-do-do-do, do-do-do</i>

18:58.330 --> 19:01.266
<i>Do-do-do, do-do-do-do-do</i>

19:01.267 --> 19:03.335
<i>Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>

19:03.336 --> 19:05.303
<i> Do-do-do-do, do-do-do</i>

19:05.304 --> 19:09.776
<i>Do-do-do, do-do-do-do-do</i>

19:16.449 --> 19:18.349
Stewie, what the hell's going on?

19:18.350 --> 19:19.817
We're back in Quahog?

19:19.818 --> 19:21.987
- We are, Brian.
- Why? What happened?

19:21.988 --> 19:24.456
You're an enormously important
part of my life, Brian,

19:24.457 --> 19:26.624
and I couldn't bear
the thought of losing you.

19:26.625 --> 19:28.793
I assumed it unlikely
you'd change your mind,

19:28.794 --> 19:31.863
so I added the fans
from many, many Dell laptops

19:31.864 --> 19:33.198
to the back of my Big Wheel

19:33.199 --> 19:35.700
so I could simply
tow everyone back to land.

19:35.701 --> 19:36.701
Wow.

19:36.702 --> 19:37.969
Thank you.

19:37.970 --> 19:39.837
That means a lot to me.

19:39.838 --> 19:41.972
Well, our journey taught me
something, Brian.

19:41.973 --> 19:44.843
You can throw away just about
anything in this world,

19:44.844 --> 19:47.479
but you can't throw away a friendship.

19:47.480 --> 19:49.547
No, you can't, Stewie.

19:49.548 --> 19:51.650
Cool if I say goodbye to the garbage?

19:51.651 --> 19:54.885
You do what you got to do,
you gross dog.

19:54.886 --> 19:57.322
<i>Do-do-do-do, do-do-do</i>

19:57.323 --> 20:00.491
<i>Do-do-do, do-do-do-do-do</i>

20:00.492 --> 20:02.360
<i>Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>

20:02.361 --> 20:04.662
<i>Do-do-do-do, do-do-do</i>

20:04.663 --> 20:08.667
<i>Do-do-do, do-do-do-do-do.</i>

20:13.506 --> 20:15.739
<i>Sweet sunshine</i>

20:15.740 --> 20:19.044
<i>So, sha-la-la-la-la-la</i>

20:19.045 --> 20:20.511
<i>My lady</i>

20:20.512 --> 20:24.015
<i>In the sun with your dress undone</i>

20:24.016 --> 20:25.883
<i>Now every mile aw...</i>

20:43.035 --> 20:46.037
Sausage and pepperoni for Alan?

20:46.038 --> 20:47.204
Alan?

20:47.205 --> 20:50.208
God, that smells good, doesn't it?

20:50.209 --> 20:51.610
- Alan?
- Yeah.

20:51.611 --> 20:54.078
But, actually, I ordered just pepperoni.

20:54.079 --> 20:57.216
Can I see your receipt?

21:00.904 --> 21:04.342
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv